rs says shifting to county sales taxes could leave renters and lower income residents behind.","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"},{"issue":"Data centers","why":"Rhoden signed a law making large data centers cover their power costs, while Ahlers wants more local control over siting and resources.","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"},{"issue":"School funding and teacher pay","why":"Ahlers wants more state school aid to cut property taxes, while Rhoden says funding is above the formula and teacher pay is up about 10,000 dollars.","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"},{"issue":"Rural health care and costs","why":"Ahlers names rural health care access and the cost of living as top concerns, and Rhoden also lists rural health care as a priority.","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/09/16/inside-race-dan-ahlers-larry-rhoden-talk-key-issues-with-dakota-news-now/"},{"issue":"Economic development","why":"Ahlers says the Future Fund should favor South Dakota owned businesses, while Rhoden points to new plants near Mitchell and in Sioux Falls.","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"}],"storylines":[{"title":"Poll shows Rhoden up 20","date":"2026-10-19","what":"A Mason Dixon poll had Rhoden at 56 percent and Ahlers at 36, though Ahlers led independents 51 to 35.","helps":"R","kind":"local","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/10/19/poll-gov-rhoden-leads-challenger-ahlers-56-36/"},{"title":"Final debate in Sioux Falls","date":"2026-09-28","what":"On SDPB the candidates clashed on data centers, school funding and property taxes, with Rhoden touting a 36 percent average homeowner tax cut and Ahlers pressing for renter and senior relief.","helps":"mixed","kind":"debate","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"},{"title":"Ahlers opposes income tax","date":"2026-09-16","what":"Ahlers said he opposes a state income tax given budget surpluses and argued divided government would make the Legislature more independent.","helps":"D","kind":"policy","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/09/16/inside-race-dan-ahlers-larry-rhoden-talk-key-issues-with-dakota-news-now/"},{"title":"Rhoden touts defense jobs and new prison","date":"2026-09-16","what":"Rhoden highlighted the Data Center Bill of Rights, a new women's prison in Pierre and plans to grow defense manufacturing.","helps":"R","kind":"policy","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/09/16/inside-race-dan-ahlers-larry-rhoden-talk-key-issues-with-dakota-news-now/"},{"title":"Trump endorses Rhoden","date":"2026-08-27","what":"Trump endorsed Rhoden, and Ahlers responded that the voters' endorsement matters most and that Trump's policies are why costs are high.","helps":"R","kind":"endorsement","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/08/28/dan-ahlers-responds-trumps-endorsement-rhoden-governor/"},{"title":"Rhoden wins GOP runoff","date":"2026-07-28","what":"Rhoden beat businessman Toby Doeden about 70 to 30 percent in the Republican runoff, running on property tax cuts and experience.","helps":"R","kind":"local","src":"https://wtam.iheart.com/content/2026-07-28-rhoden-wins-sd-primary-runoff-for-governor/"}],"events":[{"title":"Property tax relief","prompt":"A new law cuts average homeowner property taxes sharply by shifting to county sales taxes, but renters may not benefit. What is your property tax plan?","issue":"econ","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715","opts":[{"label":"Relief for renters","say":"Expand relief to renters, seniors, veterans and people with disabilities and reassess residential property.","pos":-0.5,"trump":-0.3,"tone":"calm"},{"label":"Fund schools instead","say":"Put more state aid into schools to bring local property taxes down.","pos":-0.1,"trump":null,"tone":"calm"},{"label":"Defend the big cut","say":"Tout the largest property tax cut in state history and promise more.","pos":0.7,"trump":0.4,"tone":"fiery"}]},{"title":"Data center siting","prompt":"Large data centers want to locate in South Dakota, raising power cost and land use concerns. How do you regulate them?","issue":"econ","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715","opts":[{"label":"Local control","say":"Give counties more power to decide where data centers go and how they use water and power.","pos":-0.4,"trump":-0.2,"tone":"calm"},{"label":"Make them pay","say":"Require data centers to cover their power costs and any cleanup if they leave.","pos":0.3,"trump":null,"tone":"calm"},{"label":"America first build out","say":"Welcome US owned data centers and keep foreign owners out.","pos":0.7,"trump":0.7,"tone":"fiery"}]},{"title":"Answer the Trump endorsement","prompt":"The president has endorsed in the governor's race, and voters say costs are their top issue. How do you talk about Trump?","issue":"other","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/08/28/dan-ahlers-responds-trumps-endorsement-rhoden-governor/","opts":[{"label":"Blame his policies","say":"Say Trump's policies are why costs are so high in South Dakota.","pos":-0.5,"trump":-0.9,"tone":"fiery"},{"label":"Voters decide","say":"Say the only endorsement that matters is the voters' and stay local.","pos":0,"trump":-0.2,"tone":"calm"},{"label":"Embrace the endorsement","say":"Campaign on the president's backing and his agenda for rural America.","pos":0.8,"trump":1,"tone":"fiery"}]}],"debates":[{"date":"2026-09-28","where":"Sioux Falls, SDPB and South Dakota News Watch","src":"https://www.newsfromthestates.com/node/429715"}],"endorsements":[{"who":"Donald Trump","for":"R","src":"https://www.dakotanewsnow.com/2026/08/28/dan-ahlers-responds-trumps-endorsement-rhoden-governor/"}],"ads":[],"regions":[{"name":"Sioux Falls metro","f":["46099","46083"],"note":"The state's largest and fastest growing area, Republican but more competitive in the city itself."},{"name":"Black Hills","f":["46103","46093","46081","46033"],"note":"Rapid City and the Hills, a conservative West River base near Rhoden's Sturgis are